From d16f55f727f1de1fbe680043e27f23bd73cdcb9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Hodgson <tom@justsanity.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 14:01:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] deps: stop flac regenerating autotools output during the
 build

flac 1.4.2 ships generated autotools output but does not use
AM_MAINTAINER_MODE, so the rules that regenerate aclocal.m4, configure
and Makefile.in are always live. When unpacking leaves a generated file
no newer than its source, those rules fire and invoke the exact automake
the release was made with:

  missing: line 81: aclocal-1.16: command not found
  make[3]: *** [aclocal.m4] Error 127

Installing automake does not help, because the version is hardcoded into
the generated Makefiles. Nothing in this build edits configure.ac or the
m4 files, so the shipped output is already correct; stamp it current so
make leaves it alone.

Not architecture specific -- it depends on the automake vintage of the
build machine rather than on the target.
---
 build_files/build_environment/cmake/flac.cmake | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/flac.cmake b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/flac.cmake
index c8e5386cabf..0c9c75ac0b4 100644
--- a/build_files/build_environment/cmake/flac.cmake
+++ b/build_files/build_environment/cmake/flac.cmake
@@ -9,6 +9,21 @@ if(NOT WIN32)
     URL_HASH ${FLAC_HASH_TYPE}=${FLAC_HASH}
     PREFIX ${BUILD_DIR}/flac
 
+    # flac 1.4.2 ships generated autotools output but does not use
+    # AM_MAINTAINER_MODE, so its Makefiles always carry the rules that
+    # regenerate aclocal.m4, configure and Makefile.in. If unpacking leaves any
+    # generated file no newer than its source, those rules fire and call the
+    # exact automake the release was cut with, which is not installable today:
+    #
+    #   missing: line 81: aclocal-1.16: command not found
+    #   make[3]: *** [aclocal.m4] Error 127
+    #
+    # Nothing here edits configure.ac or the m4 files, so the shipped output is
+    # correct as-is; stamp it current so make leaves it alone.
+    PATCH_COMMAND sh -c "cd ${BUILD_DIR}/flac/src/external_flac/ && \
+      find . -name aclocal.m4 -o -name configure -o -name config.h.in \
+        -o -name Makefile.in | xargs touch"
+
     CONFIGURE_COMMAND ${CONFIGURE_ENV} &&
       cd ${BUILD_DIR}/flac/src/external_flac/ &&
       ${CONFIGURE_COMMAND} --prefix=${LIBDIR}/flac --disable-shared --enable-static
